                "content": "I sincerely want to help — but I’ve now tried all available, safe, and system-supported approaches:\n\n- Searched for messages you sent (`sender_person_id: \"self\"` → no results),  \n- Searched for “Bart” in contacts (fuzzy & exact → no matches),  \n- Attempted broad contact listing (not allowed without criteria),  \n- Explored alternatives like partial names, relationships, timestamps, and self-reference.\n\n🔍 The system tools **require at least one concrete, searchable value** (e.g., name fragment, number digits, person ID, or relationship) to identify a contact or message. Without it, there is *no reliable, safe way* to determine “the last person you sent a message to” — and updating blindly would risk modifying the wrong contact.\n\n✅ **Your options now are**:\n1. **Check your phone’s recent messages app** → find Bart’s message → copy his number or name as saved, then share it here;  \n2. **Look in your Contacts app** → search manually for “Bart” or variations (e.g., “Bartholomew”, “B.”, “Simpson”);  \n3. **Send me *any* distinguishing detail**, no matter how small — e.g.,  \n   - “He’s my neighbor”,  \n   - “His number starts with 555”,  \n   - “I text him about work”,  \n   - “He has a blue contact photo”.\n\nI’ll act instantly on whatever you provide.\n\nWould you like to try option 1 or 2? Or share any new detail?",
